WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.270
Just because a director is willing to push
the boundaries of decency in the name of entertainment

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.300
doesn't mean they're guaranteed to get away
with it.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.600
Sometimes, studios are forced to drop controversial
scenes entirely, either to get a better rating,

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.960
or because of public outcry.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.100
Here's a look at some offensive movie scenes
you never got to see.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.700
It's infamous orgy

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.900
Anyone who's seen Andy Muschietti's adaptation
of Stephen King classic It knows that it's

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:29.529
plenty disturbing as it is, but if True Detective
creator Cary Fukunaga had been left in charge,

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.860
things would have been a lot creepier.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.320
According to The Telegraph, Fukunaga, who
dropped out of the project in 2015 due to

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:39.170
creative differences, put together a screenplay
that "horrified" the parents of prospective

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.040
child actors.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.040
The studio responded by completely cutting
two of the most offensive scenes in the script.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.100
Neither were as shocking, though, as a scene
from the book that was cut from both the 2017

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.899
film and 1990 TV mini-series because it featured
the children having an orgy as a rite of passage

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.720
into adulthood.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:55.480
No joke.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.679
King responded to questions about the scene
with a statement saying "times have changed

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.300
since I wrote that scene and there is now
more sensitivity to those issues."

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.320
Divergent's eyeball stabbing

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:09.840
The first book in Veronica Roth's Divergent
trilogy contains a scene in which an unsuspecting

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.670
Dauntless newcomer by the name of Edward is
gruesomely stabbed in the eye with a butter

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:14.660
knife while sleeping.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.560
A version of this disturbing turn of events
was filmed for the first Divergent movie,

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.960
but wound up getting axed.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.659
Director Neil Burger came to Lionsgate's defense
over the decision to remove this scene, claiming

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.740
it was "cut out because it was interrupting
the flow of the story."

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.980
Gangster Squad's cinema shooting

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.680
The original trailer for the 2013 crime thriller
Gangster Squad included clips from a scene

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.100
where moviegoers are gunned down with machine
guns.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.640
Just a few weeks later, James Holmes opened
fire at a Colorado cinema during a midnight

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.120
screening of The Dark Knight Rises, resulting
in 12 fatalities.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.400
The sequence was rewritten and refilmed.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.299
Director Ruben Fleischer explained the reasons
at a press conference, saying "The Aurora

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:55.320
shooting was an unspeakable tragedy, and out
of respect for the families of the victims,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.260
we felt it necessary to reshoot that sequence,
and I'm proud of the fact that we did."

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.500
Deadpool's vulgar bar scene

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.619
2016's surprise smash hit Deadpool proved
once and for all that there's a market for

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.900
R-rated superhero films.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:12.220
Some of the most popular scenes in the film
involved Ryan Reynolds and co-star T.J. Miller

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.080
trading profane clips at the bar owned by
Miller's character, Weasel.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.580
"what, like wear a mask?"

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.080
"Yes!

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.660
A very thick mask.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.440
All the time.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.240
I am sorry… you are… haunting."

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.120
But one scene they wrote together was so over
the top that according to ComicBook.com, director

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.120
Tim Miller decided they had to just cut the
whole thing entirely.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:36.460
"In particular, there was a bar scene that
was too vulgar for even the R-rated Deadpool.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.870
T.J. and Ryan got together and wrote a version
of the scene that we just said, 'Oh my God,

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.680
this is too far.'

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.640
I mean there were so many people offended…

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.740
It was just mean and so I said, 'No.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:47.080
We don't have to do that.'"

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.280
Coulson's fate in The Avengers

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.720
Hard to believe, but the first cuts of Marvel's
2012 mega-blockbuster The Avengers actually

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.660
came back rated R. The problem?

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:00.160
According to Marvel head honcho Kevin Feige,
it was because the tragic loss of SHIELD Agent

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.580
Phil Coulson was too graphic.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.560
Feige told Movies.com, "We went back and had
to make adjustments.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:08.901
Whenever you impale somebody from their back
and the blade comes out their chest, there

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:09.740
are issues."

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.880
Murphy's massacre in Robocop

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:16.920
The 1987 sci-fi classic Robocop originally
came back with a dreaded X rating - which

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:21.320
in the current rating system is an NC-17,
so director Paul Verhoeven made some tactical

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.960
cuts to the film to tone down the extreme
violence.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.360
Most importantly, he cut two seconds of footage
from a scene where Alex Murphy, the policeman

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.880
who becomes Robocop, is massacred by criminals.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.220
An elaborate model of star Peter Weller, who
played Murphy, was created just for the scene,

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.560
but after they cut the shocking footage of
his head getting blown up, the dummy only

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.680
ended up on screen for less than a second.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:42.400
Spilling guts in Scream

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.500
Legendary horror director Wes Craven had to
fight to get an R rating for the 1996 classic

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:48.000
Scream.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.920
Craven told Bloody Disgusting that the ratings
board originally wanted drastic changes.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.930
"Initially their reaction to [Scream] was
that it was virtually obscene and that almost

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.360
the entire third act had to be drastically
altered.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.840
You know, the whole scene in the kitchen with
the boys stabbing each other to establish

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.220
the alibi, all of that."

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:07.780
They also wanted the beginning of the film
changed, so Craven met them halfway by toning

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:11.620
down the stabbing scene, and removing one
shot of a character's intestines spilling

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.120
out.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:12.960
Yuck!

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.200
Thanks for watching!

